```yaml
resources:
  registered_models:
    ml_model:
      name: ${var.model_name}  # owner: approver/admin group, NOT job_run_as_sp
  jobs:
    promotion_gate:
      name: ${var.promotion_gate_job_name}
      max_concurrent_runs: 1
      run_as:
        service_principal_name: ${var.job_run_as_sp}
      parameters:
        - name: source_model_version
          default: ""
        - name: promotion_reason
          default: ""
      tasks:
        - task_key: copy_register
          notebook_task:
            notebook_path: ${var.copy_register_notebook_path}
          # spark_python_task: python_file: ${var.copy_register_python_path}
        - task_key: evaluate
          depends_on: [{task_key: copy_register}]
          notebook_task:
            notebook_path: ${var.evaluate_notebook_path}
          # mode=prod_gate + model names via task env
    promotion_cutover:
      name: ${var.promotion_cutover_job_name}
      max_concurrent_runs: 1
      run_as:
        service_principal_name: ${var.job_run_as_sp}
      parameters:
        - name: source_model_version
          default: ""
        - name: promotion_reason
          default: ""
        # dest model_version: NOT a job param
      tasks:
        - task_key: approval_check
          max_retries: 0
          notebook_task:
            notebook_path: ${var.approval_notebook_path}
          # key MUST start with "approval"; READS Approved — never writes
        - task_key: deploy
          depends_on: [{task_key: approval_check}]
          notebook_task:
            notebook_path: ${var.deploy_notebook_path}
        # optional canary_* / metrics_gate / to_100
        - task_key: rollback
          depends_on:
            - {task_key: deploy}
            # add canary_* / metrics_gate keys when those tasks exist
          run_if: AT_LEAST_ONE_FAILED
          notebook_task:
            notebook_path: ${var.rollback_notebook_path}
          # do not depend_on copy_register/evaluate; Jobs run_if — no invented outcome field
      permissions:
        - service_principal_name: ${var.ci_trigger_sp}
          level: CAN_MANAGE_RUN
        - group_name: ${var.approver_group}
          level: CAN_VIEW
```

Batch prod: `spark_udf(..., f"models:/{PROD}@prod", ...)` or `fe.score_batch`. Dev: `@dev`.

## MUST NOT

WMR / stages / WMR webhooks; `staging` / shared catalog; hardcoded catalog/schema/table/model names in executable YAML/code; Train/EDA/XAI/Compare on prod promotion or synced into the prod workspace; **promotion/`copy_register`/cutover jobs on the `dev` target**; dest `@prod` versions from any path except `copy_register`; one SP for both train and promotion; overridable job params for source/dest **model names**, dest **model_version**, or evaluate `mode`; only-notebook or only-`.py` until the user chooses; delete the unused source tree; wire zero or two DAB task types on one task (empty tasks with no `notebook_path` / python file); double-run EDA; Genie/Playground as control plane; SDP named a training pipeline; `@prod` from train or `copy_register`/`approval*`; `ml_dev` `@champion` from Compare or train-register; auto `deployment_job_id`; Compare in prod; promote no-go or `@challenger`/`@dev`; CI copy of live `@champion` without `go_version` from the train run; CI empty `source_model_version`; same-run `approval*` read immediately after evaluate with no platform pause; make smokes depend on `promotion_ready`; fail the **train job** on Compare no-go; block `promotion_ready` on XAI failure; repair a succeeded `copy_register`; flip `@prod` at canary start, canary with no previous version, or leave canary traffic after a failed `metrics_gate` without rollback; rollback on failed `copy_register`/evaluate; secrets in widgets/params; human `run_as` on prod; unauthenticated prod endpoints; `spark_udf` after `fe.log_model(training_set=...)`; skill snippets that `set_registered_model_alias(..., "prod")` in train; standing monitors inside the train job; unbounded retrain-on-alert; unbounded raw PII in MLflow/`log_table`; invented cross-metastore copy; grant aliases with only `CREATE MODEL VERSION` (need `MANAGE` or owner).

## GenAI / RAG / agents (only if asked)

Do not replace MUST. Same `dev` train/log, dual sources, copy/register, `approval*`, `deploy`, `@prod`. Add `mlflow.genai.evaluate` + scorers; traces; prompt/agent versions as UC models or bundle artifacts; Vector Search as bundle resources when RAG; Agent Bricks / `agents.deploy` only when requested. Traces/logs follow the same ACL/PII rules. Still no `@prod` from the `dev` notebook and no “retrain the agent in prod” on the promotion job.
